# Sentinel C++ (Windows)

- C++20, MSVC (Visual Studio 2026 Build Tools). CMake is the build system; Ninja is the backend. Prefer the standard library; keep Win32 isolated in `telemetry/` collectors. Configure from a VS x64 developer environment (`vcvars64.bat`) so `cl` and the Windows SDK are on PATH. Use preset `windows-msvc-ninja`.
- RAII only. No raw `new`/`delete`. Use `[[nodiscard]]` on functions whose result must not be ignored.
- Define `WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN`, `UNICODE`, `_UNICODE`, and `NOMINMAX` at the target (CMake), not scattered in headers.
- Convert `FILETIME` with shift/or, never pointer punning:

```cpp
const auto t = (static_cast<std::uint64_t>(ft.dwHighDateTime) << 32) | ft.dwLowDateTime;
```

- Hot path (`collect()`): no heap, no logging. Shared mutable state uses `std::mutex` or `std::atomic`. Copy value types (`SystemSample`) out of the lock.
- Counters (CPU times) become rates via delta vs the previous sample. Gauges (memory) are used as-is.
- Kernel time from `GetSystemTimes` includes idle. Busy = kernel + user − idle.
